@startuml
!include style.puml
left to right direction
title Health Risk Portal - Use Cases
actor "Portal user" as User
actor "Administrator" as Admin
actor "Ollama / Qwen3" as LLM
actor "Speech service\nEdge TTS / Windows SAPI" as Speech
Admin --|> User
rectangle "Health Risk Portal" {
  usecase "Sign in / sign out" as Login
  usecase "Switch interface language\nEnglish / Chinese" as Language
  usecase "Change own password" as Password
  usecase "Record health data\nbaseline / BP / mood / sleep" as Entry
  usecase "Validate values and date" as Validate
  usecase "Browse records\n30 records per page" as Query
  usecase "View risk assessment\nmodel or measurement / score" as Risk
  usecase "View health report" as Report
  usecase "Download individual PDF" as PDF
  usecase "Export 1-50 reports as ZIP" as Batch
  usecase "Train RF / XGBoost / PCA\noptional five-fold validation" as Train
  usecase "Manage member accounts\ncreate / enable / disable / reset" as Accounts
  usecase "Configure models, sessions,\nlogin limits and Doc Pup" as Settings
  usecase "Review / export activity log\ndate filter; CSV" as Logs
  usecase "Inspect population overview\ncoverage / activity / availability" as Population
  usecase "Read selected text aloud" as Read
  usecase "Fill form from voice / file\nreview before submission" as Fill
  usecase "Request contextual briefing" as Brief
  usecase "Cancel assistant operation" as Cancel
}
User -- Login
User -- Language
User -- Password
User -- Entry
User -- Query
User -- Risk
User -- Report
User -- PDF
User -- Read
User -- Fill
User -- Brief
User -- Cancel
Admin -- Batch
Admin -- Train
Admin -- Accounts
Admin -- Settings
Admin -- Logs
Admin -- Population
Entry ..> Validate : <<include>>
Fill -- LLM
Brief -- LLM
Read -- Speech
note bottom of User
  Protected operations require an authenticated session.
  Members: subject is forced to username.
  Administrators: may select a participant identifier.
  Public language switching does not require sign-in.
end note
note bottom of Admin
  is_staff gates training, users, settings and logs.
  Reset / toggle only targets non-staff, non-superusers.
  Administrative risk view aggregates an eligible year;
  member view uses personal record history.
end note
@enduml
